{"authored" [{"question" "q-50204" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $\\int ⟨{e}^{t},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩\\,\\text{d}t.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/state.json" "file_sha256" "7607ec4719b83b778accc6f508bf9e6d3c093f93f7686b6d22ff4c580be1dacb" "basis" 1276 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-50204" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨{e}^{t},\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int {e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t,\\,\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{t}+{c}_{1},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{t},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩+⟨{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{e}^{t},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/state.json" "file_sha256" "7607ec4719b83b778accc6f508bf9e6d3c093f93f7686b6d22ff4c580be1dacb" "basis" 1276 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-50204" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0fef3f7c6ec5a49384ab0b05d33ff36c1a9b9e5d77c113689d538d21c3845ef3" "basis" 1276 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-50204" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/state.json" "file_sha256" "7607ec4719b83b778accc6f508bf9e6d3c093f93f7686b6d22ff4c580be1dacb" "basis" 1276 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-99517" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If ${F}^{′}(t)=⟨3(t-1)^{2},4\\,{t}^{3}-1⟩$ and $F(1)=⟨1,\\,1⟩,$ then $F(t)=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/state.json" "file_sha256" "7607ec4719b83b778accc6f508bf9e6d3c093f93f7686b6d22ff4c580be1dacb" "basis" 1276 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-99517" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we note that \n\n$$\nF(t)=\\int {F}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int ⟨3(t-1)^{2},\\,4{t}^{3}-1⟩\\text{d}t\n$$\n\nTo integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨3(t-1)^{2},\\,4{t}^{3}-1⟩\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int 3(t-1)^{2}\\,\\text{d}t,\\int (4{t}^{3}-1)\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{(t-1)}^{3}+{c}_{1},\\,{t}^{4}-t+{c}_{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n  \n\nThe initial condition $F(1)=⟨1,\\,1⟩$ gives \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(1)=⟨{((1)-1)}^{3}+{c}_{1},\\,(1)^{4}-(1)+{c}_{2}⟩ & =⟨1,\\,1⟩ \\\\ ⟨{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}⟩ & =⟨1,\\,1⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${c}_{1}=1$ and ${c}_{2}=1.$ Consequently\n\n$$\nF(t)=⟨{(t-1)}^{3}+1,\\,{t}^{4}-t+1⟩.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/state.json" "file_sha256" "7607ec4719b83b778accc6f508bf9e6d3c093f93f7686b6d22ff4c580be1dacb" "basis" 1276 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-99517" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0fef3f7c6ec5a49384ab0b05d33ff36c1a9b9e5d77c113689d538d21c3845ef3" "basis" 1276 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-99517" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/state.json" "file_sha256" "7607ec4719b83b778accc6f508bf9e6d3c093f93f7686b6d22ff4c580be1dacb" "basis" 1276 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-99517" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨{(t-1)}^{3}+1,\\,\\frac{{t}^{5}}{5}-1⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/state.json" "file_sha256" "7607ec4719b83b778accc6f508bf9e6d3c093f93f7686b6d22ff4c580be1dacb" "basis" 1276 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-99517" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨{(t-1)}^{3}+1,\\,{t}^{4}-t+1⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/state.json" "file_sha256" "7607ec4719b83b778accc6f508bf9e6d3c093f93f7686b6d22ff4c580be1dacb" "basis" 1276 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-99517" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨{(t-1)}^{4}+1,\\,\\frac{{t}^{4}}{4}-4⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/state.json" "file_sha256" "7607ec4719b83b778accc6f508bf9e6d3c093f93f7686b6d22ff4c580be1dacb" "basis" 1276 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-99517" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨{t}^{3}+1,\\,{t}^{4}-t+1⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/state.json" "file_sha256" "7607ec4719b83b778accc6f508bf9e6d3c093f93f7686b6d22ff4c580be1dacb" "basis" 1276 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-99517" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨{t}^{3}+2,\\,{t}^{4}{-}^{2}⟩"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/state.json" "file_sha256" "7607ec4719b83b778accc6f508bf9e6d3c093f93f7686b6d22ff4c580be1dacb" "basis" 1276 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-349193" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $F(t)$ given that \n\n$$\n{F}^{′}(t)=⟨-\\frac{4}{{t}^{3/2}}\\,,\\frac{4}{t+1}⟩\n$$\n\n and $F(1)=⟨2,\\,4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)⟩.$\n\n$F(t)=⟨${{field-1}}$,$\n{{field-2}}$⟩$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/state.json" "file_sha256" "7607ec4719b83b778accc6f508bf9e6d3c093f93f7686b6d22ff4c580be1dacb" "basis" 1276 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-349193" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we note that \n\n$$\nF(t)=\\int {F}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int ⟨-\\frac{4}{{t}^{3/2}}\\,,\\frac{4}{t+1}⟩\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nTo integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨-\\frac{4}{{t}^{3/2}}\\,,\\frac{4}{t+1}⟩\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int -\\frac{4}{{t}^{3/2}}\\,\\text{d}t,\\int \\frac{4}{t+1}\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{t}}+{c}_{1},\\,4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+1)+{c}_{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe initial condition $F(1)=⟨2,\\,4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)⟩$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(1)=⟨\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{1}}+{c}_{1},\\,4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)+{c}_{2}⟩ & =⟨2,\\,4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)⟩ \\\\ ⟨8+{c}_{1},\\,4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)+{c}_{2}⟩ & =⟨2,\\,4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2)⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, ${c}_{1}=-6$ and ${c}_{2}=0.$ Consequently\n\n$$\nF(t)=⟨\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{t}}-6,\\,4\\operatorname{ln}⁡(t+1)⟩.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/state.json" "file_sha256" "7607ec4719b83b778accc6f508bf9e6d3c093f93f7686b6d22ff4c580be1dacb" "basis" 1276 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-349193" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "0fef3f7c6ec5a49384ab0b05d33ff36c1a9b9e5d77c113689d538d21c3845ef3" "basis" 1276 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-349193" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/state.json" "file_sha256" "7607ec4719b83b778accc6f508bf9e6d3c093f93f7686b6d22ff4c580be1dacb" "basis" 1276 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-349193" "field" "field-1" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "\\frac{8}{\\sqrt{t}}-6"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/state.json" "file_sha256" "7607ec4719b83b778accc6f508bf9e6d3c093f93f7686b6d22ff4c580be1dacb" "basis" 1276 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-349193" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/blank "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/state.json" "file_sha256" "7607ec4719b83b778accc6f508bf9e6d3c093f93f7686b6d22ff4c580be1dacb" "basis" 1276 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-349193" "field" "field-2" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "4\\ln(t+1)"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/state.json" "file_sha256" "7607ec4719b83b778accc6f508bf9e6d3c093f93f7686b6d22ff4c580be1dacb" "basis" 1276 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-612" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $\\mathbf F(t)$ given that $\\mathbf F'(t)= \\langle 6t^5+2t, \\sec^2 t\\rangle.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/example-612.json" "file_sha256" "ec683e0e44404b80ace907bb8362259b54d74de85f7391fcfcca3993673ae482" "basis" 1276 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-612" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that \n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(t)=\\int \\mathbf F'(t)\\, \\textrm d t=\\int \\left\\langle 6t^5+2t,\\, \\sec^2 t\\right\\rangle \\, \\textrm d t.\n$$\n\nTo integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately. So, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨6{t}^{5}+2t,\\,{sec}^{2}⁡t⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int (6{t}^{5}+2t)\\,\\text{d}t,\\,\\int {sec}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{t}^{6}+{t}^{2}+{c}_{1},\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡t+{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{t}^{6}+{t}^{2},\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡t⟩+⟨{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨{t}^{6}+{t}^{2},\\,\\operatorname{tan}⁡t⟩+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $\\mathbf C$ is an arbitrary (vector) constant of integration." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/example-612.json" "file_sha256" "ec683e0e44404b80ace907bb8362259b54d74de85f7391fcfcca3993673ae482" "basis" 1276 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-613" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\displaystyle \\int \\left\\langle\\cos(2t+1), \\, 4\\right\\rangle \\,\\textrm d t\\,.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/example-613.json" "file_sha256" "63f6e79a69492d8dcdd580a66b619986cee3548f49cd7f536b8ba6b51b68a66c" "basis" 1276 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-613" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t+1),\\,4⟩\\,\\text{d}t=⟨\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t+1)\\,\\text{d}t,\\,\\int 4\\,\\text{d}t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For $x(t) =\\cos(2t+1),$ we calculate its integral using substitution. So, we let $u= 2t +1.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\dfrac{\\textrm d u}{\\textrm d t} = 2\\quad\\Longrightarrow\\quad \\textrm d t = \\dfrac 1 2 \\textrm d u.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t+1)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡u\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(\\operatorname{sin}⁡u)+{c}_{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t+1)+{c}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For $y(t) =4,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int y(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int 4\\text{d}t=4t+{c}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t+1),\\,4⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t+1)+{c}_{1},\\,4t+{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t+1),\\,4t⟩+⟨{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t+1),\\,4t⟩+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/example-613.json" "file_sha256" "63f6e79a69492d8dcdd580a66b619986cee3548f49cd7f536b8ba6b51b68a66c" "basis" 1276 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-614" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Evaluate $\\displaystyle \\int_0^{2} \\left\\langle 2e^{t},\\, 6t^2\\right\\rangle\\, \\textrm d t.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/example-614.json" "file_sha256" "e06cc9fbe8326e46624ec2b01d77e0253032f85aecbe56ee77695764d60d3c71" "basis" 1276 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-614" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately: \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2}⟨2{e}^{t},\\,6{t}^{2}⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨{\\int }_{0}^{2}2{e}^{t}\\,\\text{d}t,\\,{\\int }_{0}^{2}6{t}^{2}\\,\\text{d}t⟩. \\\\  & =⟨2{e}^{t}\\,\\,{|}_{0}^{2},\\,2{t}^{3}\\,\\,{|}_{0}^{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨[2{e}^{2}-2{e}^{0}],\\,[2\\cdot {2}^{3}-0]⟩ \\\\  & =⟨2{e}^{2}-2,\\,16⟩\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/example-614.json" "file_sha256" "e06cc9fbe8326e46624ec2b01d77e0253032f85aecbe56ee77695764d60d3c71" "basis" 1276 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-615" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Calculate $\\mathbf F(t)$ given that $\\mathbf F'(t)= \\left\\langle \\sec t \\tan t, \\,  \\sin(2t)\\right\\rangle$ and $\\mathbf F(0)=\\langle 0,\\, 0\\rangle.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/example-615.json" "file_sha256" "6012dbcb57e1484eacbc19e8f20cbb775bab59b29682f455a53c4b90bc903124" "basis" 1276 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "e-615" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Note that \n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(t)=\\int \\mathbf F'(t)\\, \\textrm d t=\\int \\left\\langle \\sec t \\tan t,\\,  \\sin(2t)\\right\\rangle \\, \\textrm d t.\n$$\n\nTo integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately. So, we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int \\operatorname{sec}⁡t\\operatorname{tan}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t,\\int \\operatorname{sin}⁡(2t)\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡t+{c}_{1},\\,-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2t)+{c}_{2}⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThe initial condition $\\mathbf F(0)=\\left\\langle 0,\\, 0 \\right\\rangle$ gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}F(0)=⟨\\operatorname{sec}⁡0+{c}_{1},\\,-\\frac{1}{2}\\operatorname{cos}⁡(2\\cdot 0)+{c}_{2}⟩ & =⟨0,\\,0⟩ \\\\ ⟨1+{c}_{1},\\,-\\frac{1}{2}+{c}_{2}⟩ & =⟨0,\\,0⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, $c_1=-1$ and $c_2=\\dfrac 12.$ Consequently, \n\n$$\n\\mathbf F(t)=\\left\\langle  \\sec t - 1  , \\,  -\\dfrac 1 2\\cos(2t)+ \\dfrac12\\right\\rangle.\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/example-615.json" "file_sha256" "6012dbcb57e1484eacbc19e8f20cbb775bab59b29682f455a53c4b90bc903124" "basis" 1276 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture/14037744/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-80463" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "If ${F}^{′}(t)=⟨{csc}^{2}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩,$ then $F(t)=$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14055375/state.json" "file_sha256" "de02ce81f152dc8fafd99f978fee626a5175a8933452b2bface34d3c9e8a8d46" "basis" 1821 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14055375/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-80463" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "First, we note that \n\n$$\nF(t)=\\int {F}^{′}(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int ⟨{csc}^{2}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩\\text{d}t.\n$$\n\nTo integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately. So, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨{csc}^{2}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩\\text{d}t & =⟨\\int {csc}^{2}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t,\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\operatorname{cot}⁡t+{c}_{1},\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\operatorname{cot}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩+⟨{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨-\\operatorname{cot}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩+C,\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nwhere $C$ is an arbitrary (vector) constant of integration." "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14055375/state.json" "file_sha256" "de02ce81f152dc8fafd99f978fee626a5175a8933452b2bface34d3c9e8a8d46" "basis" 1821 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14055375/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-80463" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14055375/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "04eca659e09dc9a77301cd7af598024ca582eee954e6337d97e460da43fbcc92" "basis" 1821 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14055375/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-80463" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14055375/state.json" "file_sha256" "de02ce81f152dc8fafd99f978fee626a5175a8933452b2bface34d3c9e8a8d46" "basis" 1821 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14055375/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-80463" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer/value" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨-\\operatorname{cot}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{cos}⁡t⟩+C"] "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14055375/state.json" "file_sha256" "de02ce81f152dc8fafd99f978fee626a5175a8933452