"file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14055375/state.json" "file_sha256" "de02ce81f152dc8fafd99f978fee626a5175a8933452b2bface34d3c9e8a8d46" "basis" 1821 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14055375/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-80463" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/correct" "value" [:answer.type/math "⟨-\\operatorname{cot}⁡t,\\,\\operatorname{sin}⁡t⟩+C"] "category" "ma_successful_grade" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14055375/state.json" "file_sha256" "de02ce81f152dc8fafd99f978fee626a5175a8933452b2bface34d3c9e8a8d46" "basis" 1821 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14055375/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-99378" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Find $\\int ⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,3{e}^{(2t+1)}⟩\\,\\text{d}t.$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14055375/state.json" "file_sha256" "de02ce81f152dc8fafd99f978fee626a5175a8933452b2bface34d3c9e8a8d46" "basis" 1821 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14055375/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-99378" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "To integrate a vector-valued function, we integrate each component separately:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,2{e}^{(2t+1)}⟩\\,\\text{d}t=⟨\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t,\\,\\int 2{e}^{(2t+1)}\\,\\text{d}t⟩.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For $x(t)=\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,$ we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int x(t)\\,\\text{d}t=\\int \\operatorname{cos}⁡t\\,\\text{d}t=\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+{c}_{1}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n- For $y(t)=2{e}^{(2t+1)},$ we calculate its integral using substitution. So, we let $u=2t+1.$ Then\n\n$$\n\\frac{\\text{d}u}{\\text{d}t}=2\\,⟹\\,\\text{d}t=\\frac{1}{2}\\text{d}u.\n$$\n\nTherefore,  we have\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int y(t)\\,\\text{d}t & =\\int 2{e}^{(2t+1)}\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\int 3{e}^{u}\\cdot \\frac{1}{2}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}\\int {e}^{u}\\,\\text{d}u \\\\  & =\\frac{3}{2}{e}^{u}+{c}_{2} \\\\  & =\\frac{3{e}^{(2t+1)}}{2}+{c}_{2}.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFinally, we get \n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\int ⟨\\operatorname{cos}⁡t,\\,3{e}^{(2t+1)}⟩\\,\\text{d}t & =⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t+{c}_{1},\\,\\frac{3{e}^{(2t+1)}}{2}+{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\frac{3{e}^{(2t+1)}}{2}⟩+⟨{c}_{1},\\,{c}_{2}⟩ \\\\  & =⟨\\operatorname{sin}⁡t,\\,\\frac{3{e}^{(2t+1)}}{2}⟩+C.\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14055375/state.json" "file_sha256" "de02ce81f152dc8fafd99f978fee626a5175a8933452b2bface34d3c9e8a8d46" "basis" 1821 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14055375/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-99378" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14055375/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "04eca659e09dc9a77301cd7af598024ca582eee954e6337d97e460da43fbcc92" "basis" 1821 "verification" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14055375/edb-import/verification.json"} {"question" "q-99378" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/differential/14055375/state.json" "fil